  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "dwg_free_MTEXTATTRIBUTEOBJECTCONTEXTDATA_private",
    "file": "libredwg/src/dwg.spec",
    "description": "The root cause is unsafe freeing of fields generated by AcDbAnnotScaleObjectContextData_fields for MTEXTATTRIBUTEOBJECTCONTEXTDATA without validating that the parsed object state is sane. With malformed input, this object type can carry corrupted/uninitialized pointer-like members, and the generated free routine dereferences them during teardown, causing a wild read/SEGV (seen at dwg.spec:9708 expansion). The bug is in this object-specific free logic (missing pointer/state validation before dereference), not in the generic dispatcher.",
    "conditions": "Triggered via llvmfuzz by supplying crafted DWG/DXF-like data that is accepted far enough to instantiate an MTEXTATTRIBUTEOBJECTCONTEXTDATA object with invalid internal context-data fields. During global cleanup (dwg_free -> dwg_free_object -> dwg_free_variable_type -> dwg_free_variable_no_class), the MTEXTATTRIBUTEOBJECTCONTEXTDATA private free path runs and dereferences attacker-controlled/invalid pointer state from those context fields, leading to ASan SEGV."
  },
